                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Trap House\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\nTrap House is an 8-bit looking escape a house of traps and zombies type of game. I love the fact that you can make a character and that it allows LOCAL multiplayer but the game desperately needs online play. Another Great thing it has is a Level editor, this makes the game next to endless. The game has upbeat dubstep beats and a few other vintage gaming style instrumentals that arent bad. The Idea of this game was good, escape as best as you can avoiding traps, sounds fun. The game also has other game modes such as Last man standing, Murderball and Dodgesawl adding to more hours of fun.\nThe game has dark creepy overtones that work very well for it too.\nI would say some of the menus and the way it takes forever to load the next round or restart are a downfall. \nI can't stress enough how much this game needs online play.\n\nFinal Thoughts:\nOverall the game is fun, I did enjoy playing it,  But due to the limitations on no online play, I see it hard for someone to pay $15 for it, If this had online play easily worth it. Without it worth maybe $10.\nBut Still a good game, would be 10 times better with online play.\n\nPros:\n+ DEATHS, Lots of Deaths.\n+ 8 Bit Graphics\n+ Local Multiplayer\n+ Create a Level and Character Aspects\n+ Steam Achievements\n+ Controller Support\n\nCons:\n- No Online Play\n- No Trading Cards\n- $14.99\n\nThis review is a part of Steamified's Community Reviews program and the credit goes to Steamified for providing the key for review purposes.\nFor similar Steamified Reviews and Giveaways, please visit http://www.steamified.com/. \nYou're also welcome to join in the fun in our Steamified group.",
